; Godot Mini Game export configuration example
; Copy this file to `.minigame/export.cfg` (same folder) to persist dock settings.
;
; The exporter reads and writes `.minigame/export.cfg` automatically:
;   - On dock open it restores the fields below.
;   - On successful export it saves the current UI values.
;
; All paths are relative to the Godot project root.
; The exporter validates the output directory before reusing it: a directory
; inside the project, or a directory that fails OutputGuard, falls back to
; empty and the user re-picks it in the dock.
;
; This file is intended to be committed to git (except `appid`, which may be
; a sensitive client key for TikTok). Add `.minigame/export.cfg` to
; `.gitignore` if you prefer to keep it local.

[export]
platform="wechat"
appid=""
orientation="portrait"
preset="MiniGame"
output_dir=""
timeout_seconds=600.0
